# App loading contract

Keep the page inventory in `packages/onsocial-app/src/lib/app-loading-matrix.ts`
up to date when adding or changing a page.

## State behavior

- Data already available (seed, session, SSR) renders with no skeleton over
  real content.
- Cold with no painted data → structural skeleton matching the final shell.
- Client navigation without ready data: `OsRouteSettle` / `HomeFeedReveal`
  paints the skeleton on the first frame (`cover` starts at `hold`). No delay
  before that paint. After settle, the cover fades off over `--os-motion-appear`
  (280ms fallback) and then unmounts; `prefers-reduced-motion` drops the
  cover immediately. Soft-fill / reserved seats stay opaque (or swap in place)
  — do not gate late data behind `OsPageBodyAppear` (flicker). Drop place has
  no route `loading.tsx`. A tap paints the seeded panel on that commit; the
  route must not mount a second one (Collectibles / Show pass stay put).
  Hard refresh still paints the final page once.
- Refresh with painted data → keep rows and set `is-refreshing`.
- Load more → silent happy path; late/in-flight = footer PulsingDots
  (OsLoadMore / sentinel). Never append cold skeleton rows mid-list.
  Failed append → same footer seat with retry (prefer OsLoadMore).
- Empty or cold error → in-flow state.
- Error with painted rows → `OsChromeListAlert` / whisper overlay.
- Intermittent chrome → fixed overlay or `null`; never reserve hidden flow.

## Route streaming (SSR-first)

- **Known SSR pages** (portfolio face, create form with server `searchParams`,
  seeded home): paint the complete real shell once. No route `loading.tsx` and
  no page Suspense that paints a full pending stub (avoids CLS and leftover
  Flight twins). Soft-nav without a destination `loading.tsx` keeps the
  previous route until the new RSC is ready — that is intentional, not a freeze
  to paper over with a wrong skeleton.
- **True-cold only:** route `loading.tsx` is for unknown structure (catalog,
  collection, thread cold opens). Never stack a second full-shell Suspense
  on the same URL (page fallback must not mirror `loading.tsx`).
- **Parent segments with mixed children** (e.g. `/drops` + `/drops/create`)
  must not own a full-page `loading.tsx`. Index cold lives in the panel or an
  index-only Suspense; create leaves stream their own form or leaf loading.
- Prefer RSC `searchParams` → props over `useSearchParams` when that would
  force a whole-page Suspense.
- `Suspense fallback={null}` is only valid when an already-mounted shell remains
  visible and a blank first navigation is not possible.
- Unmanaged hard load: `OsRouteSettle` starts cover off so it does not add a
  second skeleton on top of streamed content.

## Geometry

- Skeleton and production rows share layout primitives, variants, and tokens.
- Cold skeletons match live row classes and box sizes (`PostRowSkeleton`,
  `HOME_FEED_COLD_SKELETON_FRAMES`).
- Route `loading.tsx` (when present) must match the destination shell — never
  a parent index shell over a child route.
- New content requires updating the real layout, skeleton, matrix row, and
  contract/visual coverage together.
